\description{
Extracts inpatient stays (or finished consultant episodes from
\code{visit_detail}), demographics, ICD-10 diagnoses, OPCS-4 procedures, provider
specialties, and admission/discharge fields from a \code{CDMConnector} /
\code{omopgenerics} \code{cdm_reference} — or directly from a \code{CohortConstructor}
\code{cohort_table} — using lazy read-only \code{dplyr}/\code{dbplyr} queries, and returns
the wide NHS APC episode table expected by \code{\link[=hrg_group_apc]{hrg_group_apc()}}, \code{\link[=pso_flag_apc]{pso_flag_apc()}}
and \code{\link[=group]{group()}}, together with OMOP provenance metadata and a readiness report.
}
\details{
Every UK/NHS mapping assumption is explicit and recorded in \code{quality}:
\itemize{
\item \strong{Diagnoses (ICD-10)} are read from \code{condition_source_concept_id} in
\code{dx_vocabulary} (default \code{"ICD10"}). Three-character ICD-10 codes are
automatically padded with \code{"X"} when the padded code exists in the HRG4+
code table (e.g. \code{I10} becomes \code{I10X}). Free-text NLP rows
(\code{condition_type_concept_id == 32858}) are excluded by default; pass
\code{vocabulary_fallback = TRUE} to reverse-map standard SNOMED concepts via
\code{concept_relationship} (\code{"Maps to"}) for stays without source ICD-10 codes.
\item \strong{Procedures (OPCS-4)} are read from both \code{procedure_concept_id} and
\code{procedure_source_concept_id} in \code{pr_vocabulary} (default \code{"OPCS4"}),
preserving recorded \verb{(procedure_date, procedure_occurrence_id)} order so
HRG4+ combination-code qualifier runs (e.g. site/approach \code{Z}/\code{Y} codes
after a driving procedure) stay intact. Stays with unmapped procedures are
flagged (\code{has_unmapped_pr}).
\item \strong{Episodes (\code{episodes})}: \code{"spell"} (default) creates one episode per
inpatient \code{visit_occurrence} (\code{EPIORDER = "1"}, \code{EPIDUR} = stay length of
stay), matching standard HES-based research practice when \code{visit_detail}
is absent or holds ward/bed transfers rather than finished consultant
episodes. Set \code{episodes = "visit_detail"} to build multi-episode spells
from \code{cdm$visit_detail} (with per-episode \code{provider_id} specialty lookup
and \code{visit_detail_id} event linkage).
\item \strong{Principal diagnosis (\code{principal})}: supports the same five explicit
strategies as \code{\link[=omop_to_msdrg]{omop_to_msdrg()}}: \code{"status"} (default, OMOP primary flag;
episodes without one leave \code{DIAG_01} blank so HRG4+ returns \code{UZ01Z}),
\code{"codelist"} (ICD-10 codes/prefixes or OMOP concept IDs / \code{CodelistGenerator}
codelist), \code{"cohort_codelist"} (automatic per-cohort index condition from
a \code{CohortConstructor} concept cohort), \code{"all"} (multi-candidate sensitivity
analysis), and \code{"first"}.
\item \strong{NHS administrative fields}: \code{SEX} (1/2/9), \code{STARTAGE} (0..130 or 999),
\code{ADMIMETH} / \code{ADMISORC} (from \code{visit_concept_id} 262 / \verb{admitted_from_*}
\itemize{
\item optional site maps), \code{DISMETH} / \code{DISDEST} (in-stay \code{death} table ->
\code{DISMETH = "4"}, \code{DISDEST = "79"}, then optional site maps, then standard
\code{discharged_to_concept_id}, then defaults \code{"1"}/\code{"19"}), and \code{MAINSPEF} /
\code{TRETSPEF} (from \code{provider.specialty_source_value} / \code{specialty_concept_id}
\item optional \code{specialty_map}, defaulting to \code{"300"} General Internal Medicine).
}
}
